# Static-hosting cache headers.
#
# Netlify-style `_headers` file. Files placed in `public/` are copied verbatim
# into the built `dist/`, so this ships as `dist/_headers`. Cloudflare Pages
# (and Netlify) honor this format; each rule's path is matched against the
# request URL and the listed headers are applied to matching responses.
#
# Strategy:
#   - `_astro/*` and `pagefind/*` assets are CONTENT-HASHED by the build (their
#     filenames change whenever their contents change), so they can be cached
#     forever and marked `immutable` — the browser never revalidates them, and a
#     content change ships under a new filename.
#   - `*.woff2` (the KaTeX font files) likewise get long, immutable caching.
#   - `favicon.svg` gets a modest one-week cache.
#   - HTML pages are intentionally NOT listed here, so they keep the host's
#     default (short) caching and content edits show up promptly.

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/pagefind/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
